From 9deb5f46ec2ea8e09428bbe02b9dedca5caa1199 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoatium Build <stoatium@localhost>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 18:57:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ui: one-click voice join, full-width joined card, friends tab
 row
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three unrelated complaints, three unrelated causes.

Voice channels took two clicks to join: the sidebar entry only navigated,
and connecting needed a second click on the call card's join preview. The
sidebar entry now connects on the same click, guarded on inCall() because
connect() starts by calling disconnect().

The profile "Joined" card is a width=1 tile: a square with overflow hidden,
about 165px across in the modal's three-column grid. That is narrower than
the Russian heading "Присоединившиеся", so it broke mid-word -- and with no
roles, status, badges or mutuals to sit beside it, the lone tile stranded
itself in the left column. It now spans the row and lays its dates out
side by side. Its hardcoded "Stoat" label became "Account created": this is
a debranded build, and the label describes when the account was made.

The friends page filter was a 72px navigation rail whose every label is
wider than the rail itself, so they wrapped and crowded while the fixed
width carved a dead column out of an empty pane. Replaced with a horizontal
tab row that can be as wide as its labels.

Also corrects "Acknowledge", which read "Знание" (knowledge) rather than an
acknowledgement.
